-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/2d77a972-df66-5db6-8b72-9bedd00b96e0
-- title:
--   Theorem 3 (O(1/k) ergodic convergence rate) (corrected: $u^1\in U\cap\operatorname{dom}J$) — $\psi(\tilde u_t,\tilde p_t)\le\tilde\rho/t$ for monotone $G$
-- statement:
--   Let $E=\mathbb R^n$, $F=\mathbb R^m$, let $C\subseteq F$ be a closed convex cone with dual cone $C^*$, and consider (VIP) with data $(U,G,J,\Theta)$. Assume:
--
--   1. Assumption A (H2)–(H5): $U$ is closed and convex, $G$ is $L$-Lipschitz on $U$, $J$ is proper, convex and lower semicontinuous, and $\Theta$ is $C$-convex and $\tau$-Lipschitz on $U$ with $\tau>0$;
--   2. $\frac{\sqrt5-1}{2}\le\eta<1$, $0<\gamma<1/\tau$ and $0<\alpha\le\frac{1}{2(\gamma\tau^2+L+\tau)\eta}$ (the setting of Lemma 4.1);
--   3. $G$ is monotone on $U$: $\langle G(u)-G(v),u-v\rangle\ge0$ for all $u,v\in U$.
--
--   Let $\{(v^k,u^k,p^k)\}$ be generated by ALAVI from an initial point $u^1\in U\cap\operatorname{dom}J$, with $q^k=\Pi_{C^*}(p^k+\gamma\Theta(u^k))$, and for integers $t\ge1$ let
--
--   $$
--   \tilde u_t=\frac1t\sum_{k=1}^t u^k,\qquad \tilde p_t=\frac1t\sum_{k=1}^t q^k .
--   $$
--
--   Then for every radius $r>0$ there is $\tilde\rho>0$ such that for every $t\ge1$, $J(\tilde u_t)<+\infty$ and
--
--   $$
--   \psi(\tilde u_t,\tilde p_t)=\max_{(\zeta,\lambda)\in(U\cap\mathfrak B_u(r))\times(C^*\cap\mathfrak B_p(r))}\Psi(\tilde u_t,\tilde p_t,\zeta,\lambda)\le\frac{\tilde\rho}{t},
--   $$
--
--   where $\Psi(u,p,\zeta,\lambda)=\langle G(\zeta),u-\zeta\rangle+J(u)-J(\zeta)+\langle\lambda,\Theta(u)\rangle-\langle p,\Theta(\zeta)\rangle$ and $\mathfrak B_u(r)$, $\mathfrak B_p(r)$ are the closed balls of radius $r$ centred at the origin. The constant $\tilde\rho$ depends on $r$ and on the run, not on $t$.
--
--   This is the $O(1/t)$ ergodic rate of ALAVI for monotone $G$, measured by the primal-dual gap function $\psi$. Assumption B is not needed.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The bound on the maximum is stated pointwise over the product of closed balls, which is equivalent; test points $\zeta\notin\operatorname{dom}J$ are omitted because $\Psi=-\infty$ there. $J$ enters $\Psi$ through its real value, and the conclusion $\tilde u_t\in\operatorname{dom}J$ guarantees it is finite. Monotonicity is the published `GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.IsMonotoneOperatorOn`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: the initial point u¹ of ALAVI is any point of ℝⁿ → Lean assumes u¹ ∈ U ∩ dom J; reason: u¹ enters ũ_t, and without it the theorem is false: with E = F = ℝ, U = [0, ∞), C = ℝ₊, G = 0, Θ(u) = u − 1, J the indicator of [0, ∞) (Assumption A (H1)–(H6) all hold), u¹ = −1, v⁰ = 0 and p⁰ = p¹ = 0, every uᵏ (k ≥ 2) is 0 and every pᵏ, qᵏ is 0, so ũ_t = −1/t ∉ dom J and ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t) = +∞ for every t (DISPROOF.md).
--   - generalization: "under the setting of Lemma 4.1", Assumption A (H1)–(H6) with (H2), (H5) on an open set containing U → Lean assumes (H2)–(H5) on U; reason: (H1) and (H6) are not used, as in the published Lemma 4.1; every instance of the paper's setting satisfies the Lean hypotheses.
--   - generalization: the radius r = (2γτ + 1)r̃ fixed from a bound r̃ on the iterates → every r > 0, with ρ̃ depending on r; reason: the paper's r is one positive number, so the Lean statement specializes to it.
--   - encoding: ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t) ≤ ρ̃/t with ψ a maximum → Ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t, ζ, λ) ≤ ρ̃/t for every ζ ∈ U ∩ dom J with ‖ζ‖ ≤ r and every λ ∈ C* with ‖λ‖ ≤ r, together with ũ_t ∈ dom J; reason: a maximum is at most c exactly when every value is; Ψ = −∞ at ζ ∉ dom J; ũ_t ∈ dom J makes J(ũ_t) finite, which the bound presupposes.
-- source:
--   Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, An Augmented Lagrangian Approach to Conically Constrained Non-monotone Variational Inequality Problems, arXiv:2306.01214v1, Theorem 3, p.22 (Ψ, ψ, ũ_t, p̃_t, r: §5.3, pp.20–21; monotone: Definition 3, p.8)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Fixed_solutionSet
import Definitions.Def_CalamaiMore_Convergence_proj
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Standing
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Params
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_IsALAVIRun
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Supplement_Psi

namespace ALAVI.Supplement

/-- **Theorem 3 (O(1/k) ergodic convergence rate).** Under the setting of Lemma 4.1
(Assumption A (H2)–(H5) and `(√5 - 1)/2 ≤ η < 1`, `0 < γ < 1/τ`,
`0 < α ≤ 1/(2(γτ² + L + τ)η)`), with `G` monotone on `U`, for a run `{(vᵏ, uᵏ, pᵏ)}` of ALAVI
started at `u¹ ∈ U ∩ dom J`, and the averages `ũ_t = (1/t) ∑_{k=1}^t uᵏ`,
`p̃_t = (1/t) ∑_{k=1}^t qᵏ`: for every radius `r > 0` there is `ρ̃ > 0` such that, for every
integer `t ≥ 1`, `ũ_t ∈ dom J` and
`ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t) = max_{(ζ, λ) ∈ (U ∩ B_u(r)) × (C* ∩ B_p(r))} Ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t, ζ, λ) ≤ ρ̃ / t`.

Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, arXiv:2306.01214v1, Theorem 3, p.22 (Ψ, ψ, ũ_t, p̃_t and r: §5.3, pp.20–21;
monotone: Definition 3, p.8).

Formalization Notes: the bound on `ψ` is stated pointwise, `Ψ(ũ_t, p̃_t, ζ, λ) ≤ ρ̃/t` for every
`ζ ∈ U ∩ dom J` with `‖ζ‖ ≤ r` and every `λ ∈ C*` with `‖λ‖ ≤ r` (closed balls centred at `0`),
which is equivalent to the bound on the maximum; points `ζ ∉ dom J` are omitted because
`Ψ = -∞` there. The paper's `r = (2γτ + 1)r̃` is one positive radius; the statement holds for
every `r > 0`, with `ρ̃` depending on `r` and on the run but not on `t`, `ζ` or `λ`.
`u¹ ∈ U ∩ dom J` is added: ALAVI's input allows any `u¹ ∈ ℝⁿ`, but `u¹` enters `ũ_t`, and for
`u¹ ∉ dom J` (or `u¹ ∉ U`) the averages can stay outside `dom J` for every `t`, so no `ρ̃`
exists. Monotonicity is the published `GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.IsMonotoneOperatorOn G U`,
`⟨G(u) - G(v), u - v⟩ ≥ 0` for `u, v ∈ U`. Assumption B is not assumed. The dual average uses
`qᵏ = Π(pᵏ + γΘ(uᵏ))`, as printed. -/
theorem theorem_3 {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]
    (U : Set E) (C : ProperCone ℝ F) (G : E → E) (J : E → EReal) (Θ : E → F) (L τ η α γ : ℝ)
    (v u : ℕ → E) (p q : ℕ → F)
    (hA : Standing U C G J Θ L τ) (hP : Params η α γ L τ)
    (hrun : IsALAVIRun U C G J Θ η α γ v u p q)
    (hG : GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.IsMonotoneOperatorOn G U)
    (hu1 : u 1 ∈ U) (hu1J : u 1 ∈ GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.effDom J) :
    ∀ r : ℝ, 0 < r → ∃ ρt : ℝ, 0 < ρt ∧ ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t →
      (1 / (t : ℝ)) • ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, u k ∈ GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.effDom J ∧
      ∀ ζ ∈ U, ζ ∈ GoldenRatioVI.Fixed.effDom J → ‖ζ‖ ≤ r →
        ∀ b ∈ ProperCone.innerDual (C : Set F), ‖b‖ ≤ r →
          Psi G J Θ ((1 / (t : ℝ)) • ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, u k)
              ((1 / (t : ℝ)) • ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t, q k) ζ b ≤ ρt / t := by sorry

end ALAVI.Supplement
